() Tj T*
(SITE CONDITIONS) Tj T*
(i\) The structure shall be designed for the exposure condition severe as defined) Tj T*
(in IS 456:2000.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4 TECHNICAL SPECIFICATION — CONCRETE AND REINFORCEMENT) Tj T*
(i\) All plain and reinforced concrete work shall conform to IS 456:2000.) Tj T*
(ii\) All RCC work shall be of grade M30.) Tj T*
(iii\) Nominal cover to reinforcement shall be 30mm.) Tj T*
(iv\) The free water-cement ratio shall not exceed 0.45.) Tj T*
(v\) Minimum cement content shall be 320 kg/m3.) Tj T*
(vi\) Cement shall be ordinary Portland cement 43 grade conforming to IS 269:2015.) Tj T*
(vii\) Coarse and fine aggregates shall conform to IS 383:2016.) Tj T*
(viii\) Reinforcement shall be Fe 500D TMT bars conforming to IS 1786:2008.) Tj T*
(ix\) Concrete shall be design mix proportioned as per IS 10262:2019.) Tj T*
(x\) Curing shall be continued for a minimum period of 10 days.) Tj T*
(xi\) Concrete shall be compacted with mechanical needle vibrators.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(SECTION 5: TESTING, INSPECTION AND CERTIFICATION) Tj T*
(i\) Cube tests for compressive strength shall be carried out at 7 and 28 days.) Tj T*
(ii\) Manufacturer's test certificates shall be furnished for each lot of cement) Tj T*
() Tj T*
